PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

REGENT OF SIGI,

Considering:
a. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence;
b. that all forms of acts of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights so that their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and disposition without discrimination;
c. that violence against women and children continues to increase, so that protection efforts are required;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3941);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);
6. Law Number 27 of 2008 concerning Establishment of Sigi Regency in Central Sulawesi Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 100, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4873);
7. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
8. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as last amended by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
9. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
10. Presidential Decree Number 36 of 1990 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Rights of the Child (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1990 Number 57);
11. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning Implementation of Women's Protection;
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Child Protection;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2010 Number 56);
14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2010 Number 446);
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Handling Child Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 42);
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number
903. ;

With Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF SIGI REGENCY and

Article 17

1. In order to achieve the objectives of protecting women and children from acts of violence, the Regional Government cooperates with: a. the government;
b. the provincial government;
c. other Regional Governments; and d. non-governmental institutions.
2. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. exchange of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of acts of violence;
c. provision of evidence and witnesses; and d. referral mechanism for case follow-up in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) is set forth in the form of a joint agreement.

CHAPTER III

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 4

Women and children victims of acts of violence receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity respected as human beings; b. the right to complaint handling and services that are fast and affordable. c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to compensation;
g. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilities in the judicial process;
h. the right to assistance;
i. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;andj. the right to rehabilitation and social reintegration.

Article 5

Child victims of acts of violence in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 4, also receive special rights, as follows: a. the right to obtain respect and services for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to be free from negative stigma;andd. the right to obtain freedom to determine choices in deciding their own affairs after parental divorce.

Article 18

1. The Regional Government establishes partnerships with business entities in the protection of women and children from victims of violence. (2) Partnerships as regulated in paragraph (1) are carried out through: a. notification of employment opportunity information for women victims of violence;
b. education and training for women victims of violence; c. educational assistance for women and children victims of violence who have dropped out of their education;
d. fostering and increasing the economic independence of women victims of violence;
e. business facilities and access to capital.
3. Partnerships as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) are set forth in a joint agreement

