Article 18

1. The Regional Government establishes partnerships with business entities in the protection of women and children from victims of violence. (2) Partnerships as regulated in paragraph (1) are carried out through: a. notification of employment opportunity information for women victims of violence;
b. education and training for women victims of violence; c. educational assistance for women and children victims of violence who have dropped out of their education;
d. fostering and increasing the economic independence of women victims of violence;
e. business facilities and access to capital.
3. Partnerships as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) are set forth in a joint agreement

Article 3

1. The objectives of implementing protection for women and children victims of violence are to:a. prevent the occurrence of all forms of violence against women and children;
b. provide initial handling of victims;
c. provide health services for victims both physical and psychological; d. provide guarantees of protection, security, and legal certainty to women and children victims of violence, witnesses, and reporters; e. seek victim recovery and rehabilitation;
f. empower victims and reintegration;
g. conduct coordination and evaluation of handling violence against women and children.
2. Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of: a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. economic neglect;ande. restriction of public access.

