PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

Article 2

The implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence is carried out based on the principles of:
a. humanity, including respect for the rights of women and children, protection and security for victims, best service, affordable and fast, sensitivity and empathy, maintaining victim confidentiality;
b. justice, including equality, legal certainty, presumption of innocence, equal rights before the law, best interests of victims, not blaming victims;
c. transparency, accountability, and participatory;
d. tolerance and non-discrimination in differences of race, between groups, gender, religion, ethnicity, age, economic background and social status.

Article 7

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 6 letter a, include: a. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection and recovery of women and children from acts of violence;
b. implementing policies for the protection and recovery of women and children from acts of violence established by the government; c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection and recovery of women and children from acts of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection and recovery of women and children from acts of violence;
e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with the financial capacity of the Region; and f. fostering, supervising, evaluating the implementation of protection and recovery of women and children from acts of violence. (2) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent establishes a Regional action plan as the basis for SKPD and UKPD.
3. The Regional action plan as referred to in paragraph (2) is prepared by involving non-governmental organizations and parties that are concerned and carry out assistance work for women and children, with a term of duty of 3 (three) years.
4. Implementation and technical instructions for the Regional action plan as referred to in paragraph (2) are regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 17

1. In order to achieve the objectives of protecting women and children from acts of violence, the Regional Government cooperates with: a. the government;
b. the provincial government;
c. other Regional Governments; and d. non-governmental institutions.
2. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. exchange of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of acts of violence;
c. provision of evidence and witnesses; and d. referral mechanism for case follow-up in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) is set forth in the form of a joint agreement.

Article 5

Child victims of acts of violence in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 4, also receive special rights, as follows: a. the right to obtain respect and services for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to be free from negative stigma;andd. the right to obtain freedom to determine choices in deciding their own affairs after parental divorce.

