CHAPTER VII

SERVICES FOR VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 13

1. Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence, are as follows: a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal aid services;
d. repatriation services;
e. psychological services; and f. rehabilitation and social reintegration services.
2. Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), are implemented in accordance with Minimum Service Standards (SPM) established by the Government and Regional Government and implemented by SKPD and UPTD whose duties and functions are in the fields of: a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection; and d. mental and spiritual.
3. In carrying out the duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government cooperates with Government agencies, other Regional Governments, and the community.

Article 12

1. Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 9, is implemented by SKPD and UPTD whose duties and functions are in the fields of: a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual; and g. peace and order.
2. Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD and UPTD as referred to in paragraph (1), is implemented in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the technical instructions of the Regional Action Plan.

